### Description

For every certificate that is loaded from files, `BuildCertificates` starts a goroutine (`setupOcspTicker`) that runs once at start and then every hour, or every `ocspStapling` seconds. It is not synchronised with TLS handshakes:

- it writes `certs[index]` (`transport/internet/tls/config.go:91`) while handshakes read the same slice in `getNewGetCertificateFunc` (`config.go:254`);
- with `ocspStapling` set, it assigns `cert.OCSPStaple` on a certificate that handshakes may be using (`config.go:88`).

The race detector reports both. Handshakes still complete, so this is a detector finding and I have not seen a failure caused by it. The second one writes a slice header that another goroutine reads, which is why I am reporting it.

Reproduced on v26.11.9. The official binaries are not built with the race detector, so the server below is `go build -race ./main` from the v26.11.9 tag (go1.27.4); the client is the official v26.11.9 binary.

A possible fix is to keep each certificate in an `atomic.Pointer` and replace it instead of changing it. With this change on main at c4561418, the test below and the tests of `transport/internet/tls` pass under the race detector (`TestECHDial` excluded, it needs network access):

